","sarga":46,"verse":12,"english":"Some smitten sore with slaps having the touch of the thunder-bolt, began to vomit blood from their mouths, with faces and eyes turned pale.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea5eb3ad4f63a65169f7921fdd3a8f254e117ef5bb9a28f90e4c67fee887dbfb","compact":"047f84d784450b188aa0f2935b05d9d48e407af789631b14ce420ee5cdf73219","nasal":"047f84d784450b188aa0f2935b05d9d48e407af789631b14ce420ee5cdf73219"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":13,"english":"And great was the uproar that arose in consequence of Rākṣasas and monkeys emitting distressful cries and sending forth leonine roars.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.644,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e84d00148a70df0ba66b973bbe37923010c2dc8338da74a279be3c66da055e46","compact":"c81592029a11da518f36f49da0a5a2a8a9fe1de23ca51ccbab6fee69eb5be890","nasal":"e8cba5f21d4666335ad33c872d93f9c7333b417946abcb0b7ab9553f83433a11"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":14,"english":"Monkeys and Rākṣasas wrought up with wrath, engaged in treading the path of heroes, looking terrific with their faces moving about, performed deeds of intrepid courage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"05818e142546eb014d8b72e86b03e5e6f5b0d6469cdb4d16f60f7cc9aecae488","compact":"f9a9926492916db7fb1ded773b1dfcf819