nkeys therewith.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc9c4ae2103d6133f6394e2f4c2f1b61ac38c2bd3806642c01c2db1185a2a390","compact":"755629e5772c7efce58ea390dcc5d875e2bb717d0702abf50263434d9d962055","nasal":"359c198d1679f275125440550729819f7aa3fbd39fa7056a80d2735495b5158a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":31,"english":"That mighty monkey-Nila-endowed with energy, struck with those sharpened shafts resembling flames, uprooting a tree, assailed therewith the irrepressible Prahasta-who was rushing against him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c4d972c69ad34f2f43965940d46b7eddaa9b4bf2c8ce5156c4531e13073f62e","compact":"379a027feb4d9f201a00cd157817ed8f8b17f0d361d52fcccf7e50fe5fcd7199","nasal":"d7f2109661400dcefb27229ae89dd9bfef0eb8142d025e0d022e7098767fb707"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":32,"english":"Thereat, that foremost of Raksasas, on being attacked, flaming up into fury and uttering roars, poured showers of arrows on the monkeyleader.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.696,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07eeec90cb537b538df347d84cfa0b600eec9d3301e3acfec416f27932c41c40","compact":"de6f127d306f4f9163af2f32bdcedb15786f6e8dd8715b2c520a98980281df50","nasal":"de6f127d306f4f9163af2f32bdcedb15786f6e8dd8715b2c520a98980281df50"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":33,"english":"And not being able to resist the arrowy vollies of that wicked-minded Raksasas, (Nila) bore them, even as a bull bear with closed eyes a fastdescending autumnal shower. And in the very same way did Nila with his eyes closed suddenly stand the mighty arrowy buffet of Prahasta incapable of being withstood.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.787,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fda3601ed42e1992aaa37bc064c5a3a78c6c2186c8fca03e067e873c560a641","compact":"7bbdd82fdee7af896936941ed4c724a34392a6e1f1c4af29c424e5b3ba99e872","nasal":"2e0b55bf6b9d5775e0950623156d8cb1d5de4d7c32001145cc747b6d7c1049ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":34,"english":"And not being able to resist the arrowy vollies of that wicked-minded Raksasas, (Nila) bore them, even as a bull bear with closed eyes a fastdescending autumnal shower. And in the very same way did Nila with his eyes closed suddenly stand the mighty arrowy buffet of Prahasta incapable of being withstood.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdb3bd1c72378e3a9e06a2707a18b37b82c64574015f1a83173f12c39bec40a9","compact":"4afe50c54655b54c50d91a033c5b371347d018f84325241a12bffee306187ebe","nasal":"4afe50c54655b54c50d91a033c5b371347d018f84325241a12bffee306187ebe"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":35,"english":"And wrought up with rage, the exceedingly strong and mighty Nila with a giant Sala slew the steeds of Prahasta.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.727,"method":"shared-s