iger, and alsò striving like a lion and a tiger.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"040e7cc5a421817fd68cf00dcf3cda379e89ba005d0ca484df9a06f82ebd91f2","compact":"6541cfc8be49e89f01c55cf801b6f39a1853dc7339c436d31aa8055e3adc8cb1","nasal":"6630afd1a8f542c82f975ea6097fad110301a695ea4bec95ff05464a06b971e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":39,"english":"Endowed with victorious vigour, those heroes, never knowing to desist from fight, were eager for fame, even like Vrtra and Vasava (fighting).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63d2d553427b77b21e49a76d6853b954ae322424d1e34437a24e7c09685ed2e6","compact":"86deaccadcd97ac77aeeec5966f9b1cd045866028df8bfab65586f8bde1aa37b","nasal":"be2cd6815a69b37d693de2678dfe038f2e61602af4989c43c0724922fef998e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":40,"english":"Then Prahasta putting forth his dearest effort, hit Nila on the temples with a mace; and the blood began to flow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f39335dd36faf6d738409c2dda7c4f30f1418ea16f024295700e0ec8c8796ec","compact":"5f84a1f1fc699bef46f49b90aae021f0168e354d2f838b4e42c4e6d8abf238be","nasal":"5f84a1f1fc699bef46f49b90aae021f0168e354d2f838b4e42c4e6d8abf238be"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":41,"english":"Then the mighty monkey, with his person drenched in blood, wrought up with passion, discharged a tall tree at Prahasta's breast.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d1abfaa11980b746f73ad6034be7f5cfeee3c2d258b3e585ab042d729e1e10a","compact":"467d5dad10f1e96ce360d8a56809d42fae26df5d188f1402d05bec5df9b465f7","nasal":"9f12ab1f96debbf1bab2a16859389a669ca48ea5523c4f33e8f9c52874667467"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":42,"english":"Without caring for that hit, he, taking up a mighty mace, furiously rushed against the monkey-Nila.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54fbf3ceb2d9933d590fbca8b47f64263114c2bfbb9024b3dbed87e3912e78ad","compact":"5e7c7ea006bf903f626c3756c2b20121ee4187c6f0f1f8a1990e1bb6ccb639a1","nasal":"f6490cce7be89748a61a34c4f7d2a0c088122a57e6b90a446369b240ad773ad9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":43,"english":"Witnessing that enraged (hero) rushing against him with exceeding impetuosity, that redoubted monkey endowed with vehemence, took up a tremendous crag.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5366426c5a3347cdb9e0c8e508f6b097b032690514e7b627c4486e50b915ea0","compact":"82c4ed2c2fc07208748efb6a1ed6fde1717b7d8324b4ee0a09f55fad5de738c1","nasal":"ea47977d07341b52358466f04455620ad2b6416b432b9910b9b4c32096881ef9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":44,"english":"In the encounter Nila at once let that crag alight right on the head of Prahasta, eager for encounter and fighting with the mace. And hurled by that foremost of monkeys, that huge and terrific crag then shattered Prahasta's head in pieces.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34b80dce38fd4265330dccfd76b2cb61850825c4f233cbe610d57de9ac34ce8c","compact":"a127f20bcfda45473a40bfa9551156647dc1708653e5e6945754ea1d6fb1e924","nasal":"a127f20bcfda45473a40bfa9551156647dc1708653e5e6945754ea1d6fb1e924"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":45,"english":"In the encounter Nila at once let that crag alight right on the head of Prahasta, eager for encounter and fighting with the mace. And hurled by that foremost of monkeys, that huge and terrific crag then shattered Prahasta's head in pieces.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2afd5ce98c911233eabaa5f1d44ac0e89a3d4feb990cd32dff6d10ae883f1b2","compact":"dfaa7d9259ad1054adb92bfe4b68e87d4f2488d40c2dc97b61a436c5ba5fba6c","nasal":"dfaa7d9259ad1054adb92bfe4b68e87d4f2488d40c2dc97b61a436c5ba5fba6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":46,"english":"Then bereft of life and shorn of nerve and devoid of sense he suddenly dropped down to the earth like a tree whose roots have been severed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046046","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bee3e179e0f010e17a5beb29d9b5f6fd686eaef1dbdfb4413456c62c2665e6bc","compact":"bc9de9d385c133fa295ede87b445dddf5272cade8c0d409dcd4f4d8ef13523ee","nasal":"748fb63e157afa50b3d3701771e69c6e18881ca3bc30c952fc5864ff2c4c6dbc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-47","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":47,"english":"Even as fountains flow from the sides of a hill, blood flowed profusely from the person of that one, whose head had been riven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.932,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046047","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0943d74e46433368a7772d9955218aeab2511c49f129a42cb84283c306aa8fa","compact":"578531e3d3661b8d7fd27603386e00d9840a3d7165f3f075823fe57567711eec","nasal":"a127e82172a1f26fade3ac1a8a2f7e0d462f8e3bafc933b7ba467bb631322522"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-48","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":48,"english":"On Prahasta being slain by Nila, that mighty army of Raksasas never trembling (from fear). retreated towards Larikā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.466,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-58-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6046048","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"951c7f9ed401451742d7004f376520bde91cd3999c139275371996c66e0667f4","compact":"5425d9129da9a9cb0f5f5ab9f8b13eb295dcc5124fa50bd2b8c064efe58d927d","nasal":"37cded217f87f98f38e33be8b097e998bfbafa54f6530ebb43e369f6e95de656"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-46-49","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":46,"verse":49,"english":"And like waters rushing (through a breach in) a dyke, the Rākşasas could not stand their ground, on their leader being slain. And on that head of the hosts being killed